<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"> <head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>PVC Decks: AZEK &amp; TimberTech in Central MA | MCB</title><meta name="description" content="PVC decking in Central Massachusetts: AZEK and TimberTech PVC vs composite, typical installed costs, heat, weight, expansion gaps and shaded-lot performance."><link rel="canonical" href="https://mcitybuilders.com/deck-building/pvc-decks"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:title" content="PVC Decks: AZEK &amp; TimberTech in Central MA | MCB"><meta property="og:description" content="PVC decking in Central Massachusetts: AZEK and TimberTech PVC vs composite, typical installed costs, heat, weight, expansion gaps and shaded-lot performance."><meta property="og:url" content="https://mcitybuilders.com/deck-building/pvc-decks"><meta property="og:site_name" content="Maverick City Builders"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Manrope:wght@200;300;400;500;600;700&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"GeneralContractor","@id":"https://mcitybuilders.com/#business","name":"Maverick City Builders","url":"https://mcitybuilders.com","telephone":"(508) 656-7436","email":"douglas@mcitybuilders.com","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"1171 Main St","addressLocality":"Lancaster","addressRegion":"MA","postalCode":"01523","addressCountry":"US"},"geo":{"@type":"GeoCoordinates","latitude":42.4556,"longitude":-71.6731},"sameAs":["https://www.facebook.com/mcitybuilders","https://www.instagram.com/mcitybuilders"]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://mcitybuilders.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Decks","item":"https://mcitybuilders.com/deck-building"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"PVC Decks: AZEK and TimberTech Advanced PVC","item":"https://mcitybuilders.com/deck-building/pvc-decks"}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Service","serviceType":"PVC Decks: AZEK and TimberTech Advanced PVC","url":"https://mcitybuilders.com/deck-building/pvc-decks","provider":{"@id":"https://mcitybuilders.com/#business"},"areaServed":{"@type":"AdministrativeArea","name":"Central Massachusetts"}}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between PVC and composite decking?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Composite boards have a core of wood fiber and plastic under a protective cap. PVC boards, like TimberTech Advanced PVC by AZEK, are made entirely of polymers with no wood fiber. That makes PVC lighter and better at shrugging off moisture and mildew, but it costs more and moves more with temperature."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are AZEK and TimberTech the same company?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Both brands were made by The AZEK Company, which became part of James Hardie in mid-2025. The PVC decking is sold as TimberTech Advanced PVC Decking by AZEK, and the composite lines are sold under the TimberTech name."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does PVC decking get hot in the sun?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"All synthetic decking gets hot in direct sun, and color matters more than material: dark boards get hotter than light ones. TimberTech says its AZEK boards stay cooler to the touch than comparable competitor boards, but on a south-facing deck we still steer people toward lighter colors."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can PVC boards go on my existing deck frame?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Sometimes. The frame has to be sound, the ledger flashed and bolted, and the joist spacing has to match the manufacturer's span requirements for the board and layout. Older frames at wider spacing often need joists added before new boards go down."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does a PVC deck last?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The boards don't rot, so the frame and footings usually decide the lifespan. Manufacturer warranties vary by product and require installation to the manufacturer's instructions, so we give you the exact product terms in writing with the estimate."}}]}</script><!-- First-touch attribution. Runs before anything else so a click-id is never
