ata-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <a class="hd__tel" href="tel:+15086567436" data-ev="phone_click" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>(508) 656-7436</a> <a class="btn hd__cta" href="/contact" data-ev="estimate_cta" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Free estimate</a> <button class="hd__burger" aria-label="Open menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="mnav" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <span data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs></span><span data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs></span> </button> </div> </div> <nav class="mnav" id="mnav" hidden aria-label="Mobile" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <div class="wrap" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <a href="/kitchen-remodeling" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Kitchen remodeling</a><a href="/bathroom-remodeling" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Bathroom remodeling</a><a href="/general-renovations" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>General renovations</a><a href="/carpentry" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Carpentry</a><a href="/deck-building" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Deck building</a><a href="/interior-painting" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Interior painting</a><a href="/exterior-painting" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Exterior painting</a><a href="/building-restoration" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Building restoration</a><a href="/water-damage-restoration" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Water damage restoration</a> <hr class="rule" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <a href="/painting" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Painting</a><a href="/portfolio" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Our work</a><a href="/areas-we-serve" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Areas we serve</a> <a href="/about" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>About</a><a href="/contact" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Free estimate</a> <a class="mnav__tel" href="tel:+15086567436" data-ev="phone_click" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>(508) 656-7436</a> </div> </nav> </header> <script type="module">var e=document.querySelector(`.hd__burger`),t=document.getElementById(`mnav`);e?.addEventListener(`click`,()=>{let n=e.getAttribute(`aria-expanded`)===`true`;e.setAttribute(`aria-expanded`,String(!n)),t&&(t.hidden=n),e.setAttribute(`aria-label`,n?`Open menu`:`Close menu`)});</script> <main id="main" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <section class="top wrap-wide" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <div data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>/</span> <a href="/deck-building" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Decks</a></nav> <h1 data-astro-cid-j5amansv>PVC Decks: AZEK and TimberTech Advanced PVC</h1> <p class="cost" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Typical Central MA range: <strong data-astro-cid-j5amansv>$70–$115 per sq ft of deck installed</strong></p> <p class="lead" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>All-plastic boards with no wood fiber. The low-upkeep pick for shaded, damp lots and pool decks.</p> <a class="btn" href="#estimate" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Book a free in-home consultation</a> </div> <figure data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <img src="/ideas/pvc-decks-main.webp" alt="Design idea: light grey PVC deck with a contrasting darker border off a shingle-style New England home backed by woods" width="1600" height="1195" fetchpriority="high" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <figcaption data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Design idea (AI illustration) — not an MCB project photo.</figcaption> </figure> </section> <article class="wrap prose" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <h2 id="who-a-pvc-deck-is-right-for">Who a PVC deck is right for</h2>
<p>PVC decking is the premium end of low-maintenance boards. Where composite blends wood fiber and plastic under a cap, PVC has no wood in it at all. We install AZEK, TimberTech, Trex and Fiberon decking, and can source other major brands on request. This page is about the all-PVC option, mainly TimberTech Advanced PVC Decking by AZEK.</p>
<p>A bit of brand background, since it confuses people: AZEK and TimberTech were both made by The AZEK Company, which James Hardie acquired in 2025. The PVC boards carry both names. TimberTech’s composite lines (like PRO and EDGE) are a different product with a wood-fiber core.</p>
<p>PVC makes the most sense when:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>The deck lives in shade or near the ground.</strong> No wood fiber means nothing for mold to feed on inside the board.</li>
<li><strong>There’s a pool or hot tub nearby.</strong> Wet feet, splashing and chlorinated water are all easy on PVC.</li>
<li><strong>You’re staying in the house a long time</strong> and want the walking surface to be the last thing you think about.</li>
</ul>
<p>It’s less compelling when budget is tight or the deck is a sunny, dry platform where a good capped composite performs nearly as well for less. For that comparison, start with our <a href="/composite-deck-installers-central-ma">composite deck page</a>. If you’re open to staining every few years, a <a href="/deck-building/pressure-treated-decks">pressure-treated deck</a> costs far less.</p>
<h2 id="pvc-vs-composite-point-by-point">PVC vs composite, point by point</h2>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th></th>
<th>Capped composite</th>
<th>PVC (e.g. AZEK)</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Core</td>
<td>Wood fiber and plastic</td>
<td>Polymers, no wood fiber</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Installed cost</td>
<td>Lower</td>
<td>Higher, often $2,500–$6,000 more on a 16x20</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Weight</td>
<td>Heavier</td>
<td>Lighter, easier to handle on stairs and upper decks</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Moisture and mildew</td>
<td>Good, cap protects the surface</td>
<td>Better, nothing organic to feed mold</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Heat in sun</td>
<td>Dark colors get hot</td>
<td>Also gets hot; color matters more than material</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Movement with temperature</td>
<td>Less</td>
<td>More, so end gaps and layout matter</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Scratches and scuffs</td>
<td>Cap scuffs under dragged furniture</td>
<td>Same; neither is immune</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Test samples before you pick. Drag a key across them, set them in the sun on your own deck at midday, and see which surface and color you like.</p>
<h2 id="what-a-pvc-deck-costs-in-central-ma">What a PVC deck costs in Central MA</h2>
<p>National guides put AZEK and other PVC decking at roughly $58 to $95 per square foot installed. With Massachusetts labor, frost footings and permits, a typical Central MA range is about <strong>$70 to $115 per square foot installed</strong>, including the pressure-treated frame, hidden fasteners, railing, one stair run and the permit.</p>
<p>These are typical ranges, not quotes:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Typical scope</th>
<th>Size</th>
<th>Typical installed range</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>New attached PVC deck, aluminum or composite rail, one stair</td>
<td>16x20 (320 sq ft)</td>
<td>$22,000–$37,000</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Same, larger footprint</td>
<td>20x20 (400 sq ft)</td>
<td>$28,000–$46,000</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>New PVC boards and railing on a sound existing frame</td>
<td>16x20</td>
<td>$13,500–$19,500</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Picture-frame border in a contrasting color</td>
<td>per deck</td>
<td>add $800–$2,500</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Collection matters. Within TimberTech’s PVC range, Harvest is the value tier, and Landmark and Vintage cost more for deeper color variation and board-width options. Our written estimate names the exact collection, color, fasteners and railing, and lists what’s excluded.</p>
<h2 id="what-the-job-involves-step-by-step">What the job involves, step by step</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Site visit and samples.</strong> We check sun, shade, drainage and how high the deck sits.</li>
<li><strong>Permit and footings.</strong> Footings go below frost depth, commonly 48 inches in Central Massachusetts. Confirm with your local building department.</li>
<li><strong>Frame to the board’s spec.</strong> Joist spacing follows the manufacturer’s span table for the board, the layout and any diagonal runs or stairs, which usually means tighter spacing than an old wood deck. Joist tape goes on top.</li>
<li><strong>Layout for movement.</strong> PVC grows and shrinks along its length more than composite. We set end gaps for the temperature on install day, per the instructions, and plan butt joints or a border so boards don’t all end at one seam.</li>
<li><strong>Boards and fascia.</strong> Grooved boards go down with hidden clips; square-edge boards at borders and stairs get color-matched plugs or screws.</li>
<li><strong>Railing, stairs, final inspection.</strong> Then cleanup.</li>
</ol>
<p>A typical deck is about one to two weeks on site after the permit, depending on size and stairs.</p>
<h2 id="new-england-issues-for-pvc">New England issues for PVC</h2>
<p><strong>Cold-weather installs.</strong> Boards installed on a cold November day will grow in July. That is fine if the gaps were set for the cold; it’s a problem if they weren’t. This is the most common PVC install mistake, and it is why we follow the temperature gapping chart.</p>
<p><strong>Shaded, wooded lots.</strong> In Harvard, Bolton and Acton, a lot of back decks sit under oaks and pines and stay damp most of the season. Composite decks in those spots often grow surface mildew in the grooves; PVC gives mold less to work with, though it still needs a wash each spring.</p>
<p><strong>Snow and ice.</strong> Shovel with a plastic blade, not metal. Check the manufacturer’s care guide before using any ice melt.</p>
<p><strong>Older homes.</strong> On the older colonials in Concord and Acton, the ledger location often means removing clapboards painted before 1978. Disturbing that paint falls under EPA lead-safe rules. Ask any contractor for their lead-safe certification in writing before that work starts.</p>
<h2 id="how-to-choose">How to choose</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Budget first, sunny lot:</strong> capped composite.</li>
<li><strong>Shade, moisture, pool, or you want the lightest board to carry up to a second-story deck:</strong> PVC.</li>
<li><strong>Color:</strong> go lighter on south and west exposures.</li>
<li><strong>Width:</strong> mixing board widths looks good on a larger deck and costs more in layout time.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="what-to-ask-any-deck-contractor-about-pvc">What to ask any deck contractor about PVC</h2>
<ul>
<li>Which exact collection and color is in the price?</li>
<li>How will you set end gaps for the install-day temperature?</li>
<li>What joist spacing does this board need, and does my existing frame meet it?</li>
<li>Are the fasteners the manufacturer’s system?</li>
<li>What are the manufacturer’s installation requirements tied to its warranty?</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="next-step">Next step</h2>
<p>If PVC is on your list, we’ll come out for a free consultation: check sun and shade, measure, bring AZEK and composite samples side by side, and follow up with a written estimate that itemises the scope, the exact products and what’s excluded.</p>
 <section class="faq" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <h2 data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Common questions</h2> <details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>What is the difference between PVC and composite decking?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Composite boards have a core of wood fiber and plastic under a protective cap. PVC boards, like TimberTech Advanced PVC by AZEK, are made entirely of polymers with no wood fiber. That makes PVC lighter and better at shrugging off moisture and mildew, but it costs more and moves more with temperature.</p></details><details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Are AZEK and TimberTech the same company?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Yes. Both brands were made by The AZEK Company, which became part of James Hardie in mid-2025. The PVC decking is sold as TimberTech Advanced PVC Decking by AZEK, and the composite lines are sold under the TimberTech name.</p></details><details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Does PVC decking get hot in the sun?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>All synthetic decking gets hot in direct sun, and color matters more than material: dark boards get hotter than light ones. TimberTech says its AZEK boards stay cooler to the touch than comparable competitor boards, but on a south-facing deck we still steer people toward lighter colors.</p></details><details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Can PVC boards go on my existing deck frame?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Sometimes. The frame has to be sound, the ledger flashed and bolted, and the joist spacing has to match the manufacturer&#39;s span requirements for the board and layout. Older frames at wider spacing often need joists added before new boards go down.</p></details><details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>How long does a PVC deck last?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>The boards don&#39;t rot, so the frame and footings usually decide the lifespan. Manufacturer warranties vary by product and require installation to the manufacturer&#39;s instructions, so we give you the exact product terms in writing with the estimate.</p></details> </section> </article> <section class="wrap-wide more" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <h2 data-astro-cid-j5amansv>More deck ideas</h2> <ul data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <li data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/deck-building/pressure-treated-decks" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><img src="/ideas/pressure-treated-decks-detail.webp" alt="Design idea: close-up of pressure-treated deck boards with face screws in a straight line over a joist" width="800" height="800" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><span data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Pressure-Treated Wood Decks</span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/deck-building/deck-railings-and-stairs" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><img src="/ideas/deck-railings-and-stairs-detail.webp" alt="Design idea: close-up of a black aluminum baluster railing meeting a white composite post with a solid rail cap" width="800" height="800" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><span data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Deck Railings and Stairs</span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/deck-building/deck-repair-and-rebuilds" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><img src="/ideas/deck-repair-and-rebuilds-detail.webp" alt="Design idea: close-up of a deck ledger bolted to a house rim with metal flashing tucked behind the siding" width="800" height="800" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><span data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Deck Repair and Rebuilds</span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/deck-building/multi-level-decks-and-pergolas" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><img src="/ideas/multi-level-decks-and-pergolas-detail.webp" alt="Design idea: close-up of open-top pergola rafter tails and a built-in deck bench with a planter box" width="800" height="800" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><span data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Multi-Level Decks and Pergolas</span></a></li> </ul> <p data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/deck-building" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Back to decks</a></p> </section> <div id="estimate" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><form class="ef" id="estimate-form" novalidate data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-name" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Name <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <input id="ef-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-name" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Please tell us your name.</p> </div> <div class="ef__grid" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-phone" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Phone <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <input id="ef-phone" name="phone" type="tel" inputmode="tel" autocomplete="tel" required data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-phone" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>We need a phone number to reach you.</p> </div> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-email" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Email</label> <input id="ef-email" name="email" type="email" inputmode="email" autocomplete="email" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-email" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>That email address doesn't look right.</p> </div> </div> <div class="ef__grid" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-town" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Project town <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <input id="ef-town" name="town" type="text" autocomplete="address-level2" required data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-town" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Which town is the project in?</p> </div> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-type" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Project type <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <select id="ef-type" name="projectType" required data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <option value="" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Choose one…</option> <option value="Kitchen remodeling" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Kitchen remodeling</option><option value="Bathroom remodeling" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Bathroom remodeling</option><option value="General renovations" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>General renovations</option><option value="Carpentry" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Carpentry</option><option value="Deck building" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Deck building</option><option value="Interior painting" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Interior painting</option><option value="Exterior painting" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Exterior painting</option><option value="Building restoration" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Building restoration</option><option value="Water damage restoration" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Water damage restoration</option> <option value="Multiple / not sure" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Multiple, or not sure yet</option> </select> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-type" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Please pick the closest match.</p> </div> </div> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-details" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Project details <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <textarea id="ef-details" name="projectDetails" rows="5" required placeholder="What you want done, roughly when, and anything you already know about the space." data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn></textarea> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-details" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>A sentence or two is plenty.</p> </div> <div class="ef__grid" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-timing" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Desired timing</label> <select id="ef-timing" name="timing" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <option value="" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>No strong preference</option> <option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>As soon as possible</option><option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Within 1–3 months</option> <option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Within 3–6 months</option><option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Later this year</option> <option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Just planning / budgeting</option> </select> </div> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-contact" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Preferred contact</label> <select id="ef-contact" name="preferredContact" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Phone call</option><option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Text message</option><option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Email</option> </select> </div> </div> <!-- Honeypot. Off-screen, aria-hidden, never focusable. --> <div class="ef__hp" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-company" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Company</label> <input id="ef-company" name="company" type="text" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> </div> <p class="ef__consent" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>
By sending this you agree we can contact you about your project by phone, text or email.
    Message rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out of texts at any time. We don't sell your details.
</p> <button class="btn ef__submit" type="submit" data-ev="form_submit" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Send it over</button> <p class="ef__note" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>We read every one of these. Prefer to talk?
<a href="tel:+15086567436" data-ev="phone_click" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>(508) 656-7436</a>.</p> <p class="ef__fail" id="ef-fail" role="alert" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn></p> </form> <div class="ef__ok" id="ef-ok" role="status" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <h3 data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Got it.</h3> <p data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Your details are with us. We'll be in touch to arrange a look at the project.
     If it's urgent, call <a href="tel:+15086567436" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>(508) 656-7436</a>.</p> </div> <script>(function(){const CRM = {"endpoint":"https://backend.leadconnectorhq.com/external-tracking/events","locationId":"b5lmCvdlpVkhC4JOVBjd","trackingId":"tk_e76468050a3e42e0b65b2fa5b3c87a7f"};
const PHONE = "(508) 656-7436";
const EMAIL = "douglas@mcitybuilders.com";

  const form = document.getElementById('estimate-form');
  const okBox = document.getElementById('ef-ok');
  const failBox = document.getElementById('ef-fail');
  if (form) {
    const started = Date.now();
    let announcedStart = false;
    form.addEventListener('input', () => {
      if (!announcedStart && typeof gtag === 'function') {
        announcedStart = true;
        gtag('event', 'form_start', { form_id: 'mcb_estimate' });   // no field contents
      }
    }, { once: false });

    const showErr = (el, on) => {
      el.setAttribute('aria-invalid', String(on));
      const p = form.querySelector('[data-err="' + el.id + '"]');
      if (p) p.hidden = !on;
    };

    form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      failBox.hidden = true;

      // --- validation with real messages, focus moved to the first problem
      let firstBad = null;
      for (const el of form.querySelectorAll('[required]')) {
        const bad = !el.value.trim();
        showErr(el, bad);
        if (bad && !firstBad) firstBad = el;
      }
      const em = form.querySelector('#ef-email');
      const emBad = em.value.trim() !== '' && !/^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]{2,}$/.test(em.value.trim());
      showErr(em, emBad);
      if (emBad && !firstBad) firstBad = em;
      if (firstBad) { firstBad.focus(); return; }

      // --- bot gates: hidden field filled, or submitted faster than a human types
      const fd = new FormData(form);
      if (String(fd.get('company') || '').trim() !== '' || Date.now() - started < 3000) {
        form.hidden = true; okBox.hidden = false; return;   // silent, nothing sent
      }

      const btn = form.querySelector('.ef__submit');
      const label = btn.textContent;
      btn.textContent = 'Sending…'; btn.disabled = true;

      let ss = null; try { ss = sessionStorage; } catch (_) {}
      const attr = (k) => { try { return (ss && ss.getItem('mcb_' + k)) || ''; } catch (_) { return ''; } };

      const payload = {
        type: 'external_form_submission',
        timestamp: Date.now(),
        formId: 'Estimate Request',
        formData: {
          full_name: fd.get('name'),
          phone: fd.get('phone'),
          email: fd.get('email') || '',          // logical OR. Not a pipe.
          'contact.project_details': fd.get('projectDetails'),
          project_town: fd.get('town'),
          project_type: fd.get('projectType'),
          timing: fd.get('timing') || '',
          preferred_contact: fd.get('preferredContact') || '',
          utm_source: attr('utm_source'), utm_medium: attr('utm_medium'),
          utm_campaign: attr('utm_campaign'), utm_term: attr('utm_term'),
          utm_content: attr('utm_content'), gclid: attr('gclid'), fbclid: attr('fbclid'),
          landing_page: attr('mcb_landing') || attr('landing'),
          referrer: attr('referrer') || document.referrer || '',
          Timezone: Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone,
        },
        url: location.href, title: document.title, path: location.pathname,
        userAgent: navigator.userAgent,
        trackingId: CRM.trackingId, locationId: CRM.locationId,
        sessionId: (crypto && crypto.randomUUID) ? crypto.randomUUID() : String(Math.random()).slice(2),
      };

      let ok = false, diag = '';
      try {
        const res = await fetch(CRM.endpoint, {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', version: '2021-07-28' },
          body: JSON.stringify(payload),
        });
        ok = res.ok; diag = 'HTTP ' + res.status;
      } catch (err) { diag = 'network: ' + (err && err.message); }

      if (!ok) {
        // Nothing reached the CRM. Keep every keystroke on screen, give a real
        // route through, and do NOT report a conversion.
        console.error('[MCB estimate form]', diag);
        btn.textContent = label; btn.disabled = false;
        failBox.innerHTML = 'We couldn\'t send that from the website. Please call ' +
          '<a href="tel:+15086567436">' + PHONE + '</a> or email ' +
          '<a href="mailto:' + EMAIL + '">' + EMAIL + '</a>. ' +
          'Everything you typed is still in the form above.';
        failBox.hidden = false;
        failBox.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
        return;
      }

      if (typeof gtag === 'function') {
        gtag('event', 'generate_lead', { form_id: 'mcb_estimate', lead_source: 'website_estimate_form' });
      }
      form.hidden = true; okBox.hidden = false;
      okBox.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
      okBox.querySelector('h3').setAttribute('tabindex', '-1');
      okBox.querySelector('h3').focus();
    });
  }
})();</script></div> </main> <footer class="ft" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <div class="wrap" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <div class="ft__top" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <div data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <span class="eyebrow" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Maverick City Builders</span> <p class="ft__pitch" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>General contracting and remodeling across Massachusetts.</p> <a class="btn btn--onDark" href="/contact" data-ev="estimate_cta" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Request an estimate</a> </div> <nav aria-label="Services" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><h2 class="ft__h" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Services</h2> <ul data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/kitchen-remodeling" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Kitchen remodeling</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/bathroom-remodeling" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Bathroom remodeling</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/general-renovations" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>General renovations</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/carpentry" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Carpentry</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/deck-building" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Deck building</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/interior-painting" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Interior painting</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/exterior-painting" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Exterior painting</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/building-restoration" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Building restoration</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/water-damage-restoration" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Water damage restoration</a></li></ul> </nav> <nav aria-label="Company" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><h2 class="ft__h" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Company</h2> <ul data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/about" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>About</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/portfolio" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Our work</a></li> <li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/areas-we-serve" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Areas we serve</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/blog" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Articles</a></li> <li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/contact" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Contact</a></li> </ul> </nav> <div data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><h2 class="ft__h" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Contact</h2> <address class="ft__nap" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <a href="tel:+15086567436" data-ev="phone_click" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>(508) 656-7436</a> <a href="mailto:douglas@mcitybuilders.com" data-ev="email_click" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>douglas@mcitybuilders.com</a> <span data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>1171 Main St<br data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Lancaster, MA 01523</span> <em data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Office visits by appointment</em> </address> </div> </div> <hr class="rule" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <div class="ft__base" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <p data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>&copy; 2026 Maverick City Builders &middot; Lancaster, Massachusetts</p> <p data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/privacy-policy" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Privacy</a> &middot; <a href="/terms" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Terms</a> &middot;
<a href="/accessibility" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Accessibility</a> &middot; <a href="/cookie-policy" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Cookies</a></p> </div> </div> </footer> </main>  <div id="mcb-cookie-banner" hidden role="dialog" aria-live="polite" aria-label="Cookie choices" style="position:fixed;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;z-index:99999;background:#0b0b0b;border-top:2px solid #E10600;color:#e6e6e6;padding:18px 20px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.55;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:14px;align-items:center;justify-content:center"> <span style="max-width:640px">We measure page views with Google Analytics in cookieless mode. Accept to allow analytics cookies and ad measurement; Decline to stay cookieless. Read our <a href="/cookie-policy" style="color:#ff6b6b;text-decoration:underline">Cookie Policy</a>.</span> <span style="display:flex;gap:10px"> <button type="button" id="mcb-cookie-decline" style="background:transparent;color:#e6e6e6;border:1px solid #777;padding:12px 20px;min-height:44px;border-radius:4px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;font-size:13px">Decline</button> <button type="button" id="mcb-cookie-accept" style="background:#E10600;color:#fff;border:0;padding:12px 22px;min-height:44px;border-radius:4px;font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;font-size:13px">Accept</button> </span> </div> <!-- Analytics with Google Consent Mode (mcb-consent-v2, 2026-09-18, Doug's decision).
       GA4 loads by default with analytics_storage DENIED = cookieless pings, no _ga cookie.
       Accept upgrades consent to granted. Browsers sending Do-Not-Track or Global Privacy
       Control get nothing at all. The static site does the same via patch_consent.py. --> <script>(function(){const ga4 = "G-7HXJQJL5Q2";

    (function () {
      var KEY = 'mcb-consent'; // MUST match the static site's key (hyphen). An underscore here meant GA4 never loaded on any Astro page.
      var dnt = false;
      try { dnt = navigator.doNotTrack == '1' || window.doNotTrack == '1' || !!navigator.globalPrivacyControl; } catch (e) {}
      window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
      window.gtag = function () { window.dataLayer.push(arguments); };
      gtag('consent', 'default', { ad_storage: 'denied', ad_user_data: 'denied', ad_personalization: 'denied',
        analytics_storage: 'denied', functionality_storage: 'granted', security_storage: 'granted' });
      function load() {
        if (window.__mcbTagged) return; window.__mcbTagged = true;
        var s = document.createElement('script'); s.async = true;
        s.src = 'https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=' + ga4;
        document.head.appendChild(s);
        gtag('js', new Date()); gtag('config', ga4);
      }
      function boot() { // Accept: cookies + ad measurement allowed
        gtag('consent', 'update', { ad_storage: 'granted', ad_user_data: 'granted', ad_personalization: 'granted', analytics_storage: 'granted' });
        load();
      }
      var stored = null;
      try { stored = localStorage.getItem(KEY); } catch (e) {}
      if (stored === 'granted') boot();
      else if (!dnt) load(); // undecided or declined: cookieless measurement only
      window.__mcbConsentBoot = boot;
      // Same banner as the static site. Without it a visitor who LANDS on a town page
      // is never asked, so is never measured.
      try {
        var v = localStorage.getItem(KEY), b = document.getElementById('mcb-cookie-banner');
        if (b && v !== 'granted' && v !== 'denied') {
          b.hidden = false;
          document.getElementById('mcb-cookie-accept').addEventListener('click', function () { try { localStorage.setItem(KEY, 'granted'); } catch (e) {} b.hidden = true; boot(); });
          document.getElementById('mcb-cookie-decline').addEventListener('click', function () { try { localStorage.setItem(KEY, 'denied'); } catch (e) {} b.hidden = true; });
        }
      } catch (e) {}
      // lightweight, non-sensitive interaction events
      document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        var a = e.target && e.target.closest && e.target.closest('[data-ev]');
        if (a && typeof window.gtag === 'function') {
          gtag('event', a.getAttribute('data-ev'), { link_url: a.getAttribute('href') || '' });
        }
      }, true);
    })();
  })();</script></body> </html>